<section class="faq-body">
  <div class="wrap-wide">
    <div class="faq-grid">

      <aside class="faq-nav">
        <a href="#cat-about" class="is-active">About IONIQ</a>
        <a href="#cat-ingredients">Ingredients &amp; science</a>
        <a href="#cat-usage">How to use</a>
        <a href="#cat-subscription">Subscription &amp; shipping</a>
      </aside>

      <div class="faq-col">

        <div class="faq-section" id="cat-about">
          <h2>About <em>IONIQ</em></h2>
          <details class="qa" open>
            <summary>What is IONIQ?</summary>
            <div class="body">IONIQ is a daily stick that does four jobs in one — energy, endurance, focus and recovery — on a real electrolyte base. Seven labelled actives, built around Himalayan pink salt for a 750mg sodium dose, with every milligram printed on the pack.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>Who is it for?</summary>
            <div class="body">For people who actually play — tennis, padel, football, running, lifting. It replaces the four products most active people carry: an electrolyte, a focus supplement, magnesium and a recovery drink.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>How is IONIQ different from LMNT, Liquid IV, Gatorade?</summary>
            <div class="body">750mg sodium per sachet — far more than most sports drinks dose (200–400mg) — plus magnesium and a labelled focus and recovery stack none of them carry. Zero added sugar.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>Why Himalayan pink salt?</summary>
            <div class="body">Pink salt is naturally mineral-rich and lets us deliver a real 750mg sodium dose — the amount your body actually loses when you sweat — rather than the bare minimum most drinks add for flavour.</div>
          </details>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-section" id="cat-ingredients">
          <h2>Ingredients &amp; <em>science</em></h2>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>What's in a sachet?</summary>
            <div class="body">Seven labelled actives across four jobs, on a real electrolyte base. <strong>Energy:</strong> Rhodiola rosea 200mg. <strong>Endurance:</strong> L-citrulline 3g. <strong>Focus:</strong> citicoline 250mg. <strong>Recovery:</strong> creatine monohydrate 3g. <strong>Electrolytes:</strong> 750mg sodium (from Himalayan pink salt), 200mg potassium, 50mg magnesium. Full list: Himalayan pink salt, potassium citrate, magnesium citrate, L-citrulline, creatine monohydrate, Rhodiola rosea extract (3% rosavins), citicoline, citric acid, natural lemon flavour, monk fruit extract, organic stevia leaf extract, silicon dioxide. No fillers, no proprietary blends, no artificial colours or flavours.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>Does it contain sugar or sweeteners?</summary>
            <div class="body">No added sugar. Zero. The light sweetness comes from monk fruit and a little organic stevia leaf extract. Around 8 calories per sachet.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>Does it contain caffeine?</summary>
            <div class="body">No. IONIQ is completely caffeine-free. The focus support comes from citicoline, L-tyrosine and rhodiola — not stimulants. No spike, no crash.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>Is it vegan, gluten-free, non-GMO?</summary>
            <div class="body">Yes to all three. 100% plant-based, certified gluten-free, non-GMO, no dairy, soy, nuts, no artificial colours/flavours/preservatives.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>Is the pink salt safe and tested?</summary>
            <div class="body">Yes. The Himalayan pink salt is food-grade and every batch is heavy-metal tested. Manufactured to standard food-safety controls.</div>
          </details>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-section" id="cat-usage">
          <h2>How to <em>use</em> it</h2>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>When should I drink IONIQ?</summary>
            <div class="body"><strong>In the morning</strong>, or 30–45 minutes before you train to pre-load your sodium and focus. On heavy days, have a second within 30 minutes of finishing.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>How much water should I mix it with?</summary>
            <div class="body">500ml of cold water is standard. You can go up to 1L for a lighter flavour, or down to 350ml for stronger taste.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>How many sachets per day?</summary>
            <div class="body">One is enough for most people. Up to three is safe on heavy training days, in hot weather, or post-sauna.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>Will it break my fast?</summary>
            <div class="body">No. Under 10 calories per sachet, zero sugar, zero sweeteners. Will not raise insulin or affect ketosis.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>When will I notice a difference?</summary>
            <div class="body">Cleaner steady energy and focus is what most people notice first, within the first few days of daily use.</div>
          </details>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-section" id="cat-subscription">
          <h2>Subscription <em>&amp; shipping</em></h2>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>How does the subscription work?</summary>
            <div class="body">$39.99 for 30 sticks. Subscribe to save and get free shipping, or buy once — skip, pause or cancel any time.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>Can I skip a month or change frequency?</summary>
            <div class="body">Yes, any time. Log in, go to "Manage subscription," change frequency or pause indefinitely. No phone calls.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>How do I cancel?</summary>
            <div class="body">Click "Cancel" in your account dashboard. Takes 10 seconds. No fees, no questions, no friction.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>What about the 60-day guarantee?</summary>
            <div class="body">Try IONIQ for 60 days. If you're not happy, email us — we'll refund the box. No restocking fees, no questions.</div>
          </details>
          <details class="qa">
            <summary>Where do you ship?</summary>
            <div class="body">Worldwide. Subscriptions ship free. One-time orders ship free over $50. US/UK: 2–4 days. EU: 3–6 days. UAE/Singapore: 1–3 days.</div>
          </details>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<script>
  const navLinks = document.querySelectorAll('.faq-nav a');
  const sections = [...document.querySelectorAll('.faq-section')];
  const io = new IntersectionObserver(entries => {
    entries.forEach(e => {
      if (e.isIntersecting) {
        navLinks.forEach(a => a.classList.toggle('is-active', a.getAttribute('href') === '#' + e.target.id));
      }
    });
  }, { rootMargin: '-30% 0px -55% 0px' });
  sections.forEach(s => io.observe(s));
</script>
